   of Territories - Ecological Challenges of the 21st Century, Kazan,
   RUSSIA, SEP 27-29, 2017},
Abstract = {Bird synanthropization is connected with a thorough and serious
   reconstruction of their biology and is a demonstration of changes
   currently occurring in the biosphere due to human influence. Nutritional
   and nesting conditions as well as protection due to urban
   characteristics are advantage factors that affect their populations.
   Under these conditions, the adaptive potential of species can be
   realized. Adaptations to a new and in-distinctive environment appear due
   to preadaptations. The synanthropization process of species happens
   without speciation by expression of existing genetic variation of
   morphological and ecological characteristics.},
