Organization = {RUDN Univ Program 5-100; Erasmus+ Jean Monnet Project European Tradit
   Governance Design \& Environm Management Megacities Search Solut},
Abstract = {Urban living is associated with numerous risks, including microbial
   environment (some microorganisms can be pathogenic). Another problem is
   falsification of food products, food supplements, and medicinal herbal
   teas. Small invertebrates, such as insects, mites, and ticks, add to the
   discomfort of human life. Besides, some small invertebrates are
   dangerous plant pests. In this work, we used DNA barcoding and
   metabarcoding to assay food products in the city of Voronezh. We were
   able to reveal the presence of opportunistic pathogenic microorganisms
   Bacillus cereus, Enterococcus sp., Serratia sp., Staphylococcus
   epidermidis and Cronobacter sakazakii in the analyzed products. We also
   identified cases of fish falsification in the products of Japanese
   cuisine. DNA metabarcoding of bee pollen (food supplement) revealed the
   presence of Enterobacteriaceae species in 17 out of 18 assayed samples,
   thereby indicating potential danger of this supplement for human health.
   We also proved that DNA barcoding can be used for identification of
   insect and mite pest species.},
