Title = {Restoration of tropical urban lakes: Case study - Lake Pampulha, Brazil},
Booktitle = {Restoration and Management of Tropical Eutrophic Lakes},
Year = {2005},
Pages = {405-421},
Note = {International Workshop on Restoration and Management of Eutrophic Lakes,
   Kunming, PEOPLES R CHINA, 2001},
Abstract = {This chapter describes the restoration of a tropic urban reservoir in
   Brazil, with emphasis on the engineering processes that have been
   adopted for this purpose. The main characteristics of tropical lentic
   systems are discussed in the beginning of the text. Here the most
   relevant feature is the accelerated dynamics in the functioning of warm
   water environments. The results of a broad-based research carried out in
   Brazil, regarding morphological informations of over 600 lakes and
   reservoirs, are covered next, with the objective of stressing the
   importance of physical aspects in the management of tropical aquatic
   systems. Finally, there is the presentation of preventive and corrective
   measures implemented in order to restore Lake Pampulha, an urban
   reservoir situated in the city of Belo Horizonte, Brazil (A: 2,6 km 2;
   V: 14 mi m(3); max. depth: 16 m). The adopted preventive techniques were
   sewage diversion, slums urbanization, construction of sedimentation
   basins and of a new sanitary landfill. The corrective processes were
   mostly directed to the eutrophication control: sediment dredging, deep
   water discharge, macrophyte removal and hydroseeding for erosion
   control.},
