Abstract = {This paper analyzes conservation behaviour of university students. Data
   is gathered in 2010 from 248 full-time UiTM Shah Alam students of
   different fields of study using survey questionnaire. The study analyses
   conservation behaviour of university students in relation to specific
   socio-demographic characteristics. Specifically, analysis includes
   investigation into the relationship of gender, urban-rural strata of
   student's background, parents' highest education level and fields of
   study with conservation behaviour around the campus area and in their
   lifestyle. Results show significant relationship between conservation
   behaviour of university students with rural background and parents with
   school education as their highest education level. (C) 2012 Published by
