Pages = {2684-2687},
Note = {1st International Conference on Energy and Environmental Protection
   (ICEEP 2012), Hohhot, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 23-24, 2012},
Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ},
Abstract = {``Villages inside cities{''} is a particular phenomenon caused by the
   dual structure of urban-rural, and poor planning which occurs in the
   process of the rapid urbanization. This paper introduces the
   distribution of villages inside cities in Guilin, causes, the resources,
   ecological and environmental problems which living environment faced to,
   and the recommendations and measures of the village inside cities in
   Guilin, hoping there will have some reference to the transformation in
   the future.
   Since 1980s, along with the continuous advancement of Chinese reform and
   openness and rapid development of urbanization, the urban fringe zones
   in many cities are varying some ``villages inside cities{''} on some
   degree, meanwhile, it brings a range of environmental and social issues
   such as resources, ecological and many other aspects, which restricts
   the sustainable development seriously. Guilin is a historical and
   cultural city and a tourist city. Although the city expands slowly, out
   of protecting the area, attractions and the natural landscape, it
   retains a large number of original villages and rural farmland in the
   east coast of Li River, Qingxing Park and the surrounding of Chuanshan
   Park. However, with the rapid progress of urbanization and the
   construction of ring road, these areas have been incorporated into the
   city territory, thus there forms a number of ``villages inside
   cities{''}, and many problems occurs correspondingly, according to
   these, many aspects of such problems are discussed.},
