   KOREA, AUG 25-27, 2014},
Organization = {Assoc Malaysian Environm Behav Researchers},
Abstract = {This paper intends to fill the gaps between community facilities
   planning in the neighbourhood area with walkability using GIS approach
   to encourage more sustainable environment for all. Several studies have
   outlined that there are three main neighbourhood environment indices
   that can contribute towards improving neighbourhood walkability that are
   (1) residential density; (2) Landuse mixed and (3) street connectivity.
   The aim of this paper is to determine the neighbourhood environments
   indices that can influence neighbourhood walkability to reach the
   community facilities provided in the neighbourhood area. GIS approach
   was used to utilize neighbourhood environment through layout plan. The
   significant findings in the paper will show that residential density,
   street connectivity and nonresidents components of mixed land use do
   affect the neighborhood walkability. (C) 2015 Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
