Organization = {CNR, Grp Nazl Cibernet \& Biofis; Elsag Bailey; Reg Siciliana; Palermo
   Univ, Ctr Interdipt Tecnol Conoscenza; Pavia Univ, Ctr Interdipt Sci
   Cognit; Italian Presidency European Union 1996; ACM SIGARCH; ACM SIGART;
   ACM SIGCHI},
Abstract = {Sonic and ultrasonic waves can be exploited by robots to perceive the
   environment.
   The main choice is between two basic operating modes: passive and
   active. In the former mode, one or more probes detect ultrasounds
   originating from natural or artificial sources, trying to establish
   their position. In the latter, the probe, or probes, emit ultrasound
   beams, generally as wave-trains, and detect the so induced echoes,
   trying to identify the features of the encountered obstacles.
   In this paper, information is given about the main features of the sound
   propagation in air and of the required transducers, and about the
   principal environment parameters that can be evaluated by means of
   passive and active techniques.},
