   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Use of electrical and electromagnetic prospecting in urban areas is
   different to that in natural ones. In urban areas the industrial
   electromagnetic noise is generally higher and the underground structure
   is more complex. Engineering and geotechnical problems there are also
   specific.
   The most useful methods for these areas are the Vertical Electrical
   Sounding, the Frequency Domain Electromagnetic Methods and the Mise-a-la
   Masse Method, etc. A brief theory of the methods is described,
   particularities of the field work technology, facilities and equipment
   are developed, the data acquisition and interpretation features are
   discussed.
   Some case study (engineer communications investigation, gasoline
   contamination prospecting) at the Saint-Petersburg area are also
   described.},
