   Informat Technol},
Abstract = {Human society has adapted to the technologies, but many species on the
   earth are not able to survive because of the changes in technology. It
   is also very quickly moving away from the nature. In the last
   millennium, every individual would be aware of a bird which is common in
   his locality. The new millennium has given us many new technologies,
   which help astronauts in space stations through social networking tools
   like twitter. But, the last decade also has made human society mostly in
   urban areas to get isolated from the sparrows. Definitely, there will be
   different opinions to a question ``whether technology has made humans
   move away from natural world and environment in the era of ever changing
   technology{''}. Technology also has the huge potential to reverse the
   trend and play an important role in preservation of environment and
   planet earth. New media is making environmental activism more popular
   among the people interested in the greener issues. Hence generating
   great deal of awareness for the realization of one of the main goals of
   the Millennium Developmental Goals (MGD) which have to be achieved by
   2015 i.e. Ensuring Environmental Sustainability. Online media or the Web
   medium is the one which can be nearer to many people,through the tools
   like e-mail, social networking, websites, mobile applications etc.The
   message can be repeated in much better form than any another form of
   traditional medium as it has a viral effect. Social Networking is one of
   the popular tools for the messages to environmentalists to masses spread
   across the world.},
