   ENVIRONMENT},
Year = {2000},
Pages = {404-410},
Note = {International Symposium on Hydrogeology and the Environment (HE 2000),
   WUHAN, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 17-21, 2000},
Organization = {China Univ Geosci},
Abstract = {Since 1992, in the Radioecological Center research work has been
   performed on potable groundwater monitoring in the Kyiv urban
   agglomeration (KUA) with a population of about 3 million people. The
   results obtained allow to state that groundwater radionuclide
   contamination of the given territory (caused by Chernobyl NPP accident)
   is 50 similar to 100 times less than the tentative water quality
   standards. At the same time, the chemical contamination of two upper
   aquifers is rather significant. The results of studies presented in this
   paper describe the groundwater conditions in KUA. These data serve as
   the basis for taking administrative decisions and working out ecological
   measures.},
