   15-18, 2012},
Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {The circular economy is a concrete realization of urban sustainable
   development which contributes to reduce the excessive resources
   consumption of the traditional economy and associated environmental
   pollution. The development of urban circular economy relies largely on
   ecological-friendly economic development paradigm focusing on cleaner
   production, comprehensive utilization of resources, and ecological
   design. With the development of urban circular economy, problems
   resulting from resources shortage in several Chinese cities have been
   solved to a certain extent. In this paper, the author discusses the
   necessity and urgency of developing urban circular economy for
   resource-based cities, and provides several suggestions to promote urban
   circular development in China.},
