Abstract = {Chemicals used as pesticides are both a broad, vital catalyst for the
   support and advancement of all aspects of our lives, and at the same
   time targets of extensive suspicion and mistrust. Spectacular beneficial
   responses to chemical technologies in medicine, agriculture, nutrition,
   and manufacturing have occurred over long periods of time. Issues and
   common perceptions of the health and environmental significance of
   chemical exposure often dominate discussion of pesticide use indoors and
   in agriculture. As those technologies have been developed and used,
   adverse effects have been observed from time to time, but that reality
   is dwarfed by subjective feelings that often outweigh reason.},
