   Biomed Elect},
Abstract = {In this paper, an Electroencephalography (EEG) experiment was designed
   to investigate the variance of brain activities during listening to the
   music with different pitch levels. The music was played at five pitch
   levels, the original one (ORI), 7 semitones low (7SL), 7 semitones high
   (7SH), 12 semitones low (12SL) and 12 semitones high (12SH). The results
   showed that in tonality transposition (7SL and 7SH), the Power Spectral
   Density (PSD) of 7SL was higher than 7SH, and ORI was minimum in theta,
   a 1 and beta 1 frequency bands. While in the octave transposition, the
   12SL PSD was higher than 12SH and the ORI in 0 and a I The differences
   were significant (P<0.05). The results indicated that the variance in
   pitch perception can be reflected by EEG, and depends on the
   psychological distance between transposed melodies and original one.},
