Note = {International Workshop on Intelligent Information Technology (2WINTECH),
   Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, OCT 20-22, 2016},
Abstract = {The purpose of this study is to examine modern applicability of the
   human evaluation model (HEM). The HEM is a person perception theory
   developed by Hangi Choi, a Korean scholar in the 19th century. This
   model developed on the basis of oriental Confucian philosophy is
   composed of 5 latent variables (20 measurement variables) such as
   disposition, virture, personality, cognitive faculty, and personal
   environment. It was designed to evaluate innate elements and acquired
   parts of a person in a multi-faceted way. Therefore, this study verified
   the reliablility and validity of its construct for 554 samples. The
   scale was evaluated to using exploratory (EFA) and confirmatory factor
   analysis (CFA) were applied. As a result of analyzing the reliability of
   HEM, all of the 20 items proposed satisfied the recommended standard
   (alpha = .78-.84). Also in the construct validity analysis, the absolute
   and incremental fit indexes satisfied the recommended standard. This
   result provides academic implications which could be applied to diverse
   follow-up studies in the conginitive behavioral sciences, information
   science and pedagogy etc.},
