Number = {1},
Pages = {170-178},
Note = {13th International Symposium on Problems of Landscape Ecological
   Research, Mojmirovce, SLOVAKIA, SEP 30-OCT 03, 2003},
Organization = {Slovak Acad Sci, Inst Landscape Ecol; Austrian Inst E \& SE European
   Studies Vienna, Branch Off Bratislava},
Abstract = {From the beginning of contemporary landscape ecology the topic of
   landscape perception has played an important role. The general problem
   of landscape perception could be labeled as ``validity{''} and
   ``stability{''} of the obtained social and aesthetic data. Our study is
   focused on the stability of landscape perception and on the methodology
   connected with the problem of aesthetic landscape evaluation. Results
   from the study area Novohradske Mts am presented. We used ``actions{''},
   i.e. supported aesthetic values for each landscape area, as a feedback
   in the aesthetic evaluation. The selection principle of these areas was
   the amount of patches in natural succession in a rural landscape. Also,
   we used an economic method, contingent valuation, in order to gain
   quantitative indicators as a kind of attestation of the respondent's
   qualitative preferences. The results show relatively great changes in
   landscape perception in the natural - rural areas. Traditional
   conservation land-use was considered to be too cultivated, being similar
   to parks or gardens. On the contrary, some stage of natural succession
   was appreciated as well as the possibility of a new beginning, or
   renewal, of the rural landscape.},
