Abstract = {Universities are often situated in the centre of an urban conurbation or
   at least in close proximity. They are sometimes the major employer in
   the city, district or town and they engage with the community, commerce
   and business activities which makes them a key factor in the success of
   the city both in terms of its social construct and its economic
   viability. In addition they are the providers of knowledge upon which
   the community may depend and they create and develop that knowledge
   through research and innovation making them a powerhouse for all aspects
   of the sustainability of the urban community both locally and beyond.
   Their position makes them central to the opportunity for leadership in
   the whole area of urban sustainability. This has been recognised by the
   members of the University Organisations of the G8 and G20 countries
   together with similar associations within the developing world. At their
   summit in Turin, Italy, prior to the Heads of State Summit in 2009 they
   agreed on a declaration (www.g8university.com) relating to their agreed
   approach to sustainable development. The author was a co-author of the
   original draft of this declaration and this paper explores the role that
   universities can play in such an important topic which is transforming
   the way we think and behave in our world.},
