Abstract = {Nowadays most of teachers regard school trips as one of the most
   important forms of work with the students. Teachers put them in a
   hierarchy of importance and usefulness of the methods of education and
   upbringing shortly behind the classic school lesson: Does forest
   education fulfil its established task and how ``forest{''} - as the
   greatest gift of nature - can educate the young society? From the
   analysis of interviews and observations conducted among the employees of
   The National State Forests, selected teachers and pupils of the Great
   Poland Region (case study), it appears that the ``subject trips{''},
   understood as lessons in the open field are one of the most appreciated
   forms of school trips. Moreover, forest education of society is one of
   the priorities of the National State Forests. To know and understand the
   forest, it is not enough just to read about it or see it in photographs;
