Abstract = {Implementing Industrialised Building System (IBS) to the construction
   industry has the potential of contributing to sustainable construction
   development. However, since the introduction of IBS and its promises to
   improve the current construction method and scenario in Malaysia, the
   public perception towards its applicability is becoming an issue. This
   issue is greatly contributing to the low usage of IBS components in the
   construction industry. Low implementation of IBS will result in the
   target of achieving sustainable construction is far from being reached.
   Better public perception will create better understanding and demand of
   IBS adoption, indirectly contributing to the future sustainability
