Organization = {Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol},
Abstract = {As the base of land use system, land grading and evaluating possesses
   important status and role. It has become a very important mission of
   land management in coming future. Routine method is cumbersome,
   error-prone and low efficiency because of separating these two types of
   data. GIS, a graph and property management system, has powerful spatial
   analysis and data management capabilities. it is the inevitable trend of
   urban land grading and evaluating that GIS combined with the standard
   land price evaluation model, and make full use of their own superiority
   to complete the data processing and analysis task in the urban land
   grading and evaluating. This. paper discusses the structure and function
   of GIS-based urban land grading and evaluating information system, and
   study the design and realization method, with a view to provide the
   reference for land grading and evaluating in our country. The practice
   shows that the system possesses many characteristics, such as simple,
