Year = {2013},
Volume = {409-410},
Pages = {921-924},
Note = {2nd International Conference on Civil, Architectural and Hydraulic
   Engineering (ICCAHE 2013), Zhuhai, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 27-28, 2013},
Abstract = {Urban and Rural Planning Act strengthens the role and status of the
   regulatory plan. Strict adjustment program is needed if government want
   to revise a plan. Therefore, how to improve the scientificity and
   feasibility of regulatory plan is very important. This article
   summarizes some questions about regulatory plan from technology view.
   These questions include random entrust and difficult linkage between
   different plans by lacking of overall consideration, previous studies
   are not profound, the unified content and depth result in planning with
   no pertinence, regulating index system is standardized, and parcel
   division is not practical. Then, some specific measures to resolve these
   questions are put forward, include establishment of a unified land
   coding system, hierarchical control, zoning control and formulate a
   unified local technical requirements.},
