Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {The traditional methodology of terrain suitability assessment for urban
   construction in Yugoslav practice, was based on qualitative evaluation
   of geoenvironmental parameters. Special purpose engineering geological
   maps were compiled according to the principles, criteria and category
   and they were used as a final documentation in urban planning. The
   quantitative evaluation of geoenvironmental parameters by fuzzy sets
   theory is a new approach, both theoretically and practically. In this
   paper the traditional and fuzzy approach was described for the General
   Urban plan of Kursumlija municipality, Yugoslavia. After that, a
   comparison of results was done, from the point of view of their utility
   as a final engineering geological document for urban planning.},
